theory.intro:
A composite solid is made by joining simple solids, such as a cone on a cylinder or a pyramid on a prism. Add the area of every **outside** face. Where two solids meet, the touching faces are inside and are not counted.

[tikz]% mathsmap-solid {"version":1,"kind":"analytic-cone","radius":1.3,"projectedRadius":0.4,"height":1.9}
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
% Parameterised curvedSolidTikz: tangent points satisfy y=b^2/H.
\newcommand{\curvedSolidTikz}[3]{
\pgfmathsetmacro{\tangentAngle}{asin(#2/#3)}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\tangentX}{#1*cos(\tangentAngle)}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\tangentY}{#2*#2/#3}
\coordinate (coneLeft) at (-\tangentX,\tangentY);
\coordinate (coneRight) at (\tangentX,\tangentY);
\coordinate (coneApex) at (0,#3);
\draw (coneLeft) arc[start angle={180-\tangentAngle},end angle={360+\tangentAngle},x radius=#1,y radius=#2];
\draw[dashed] (coneRight) arc[start angle=\tangentAngle,end angle={180-\tangentAngle},x radius=#1,y radius=#2];
\draw (coneLeft)--(coneApex)--(coneRight);
}
\draw (-1.3,0) -- (-1.3,1.6);
\draw (1.3,0) -- (1.3,1.6);
\draw (-1.3,0) arc (180:360:1.3 and 0.4);
\draw[dashed] (1.3,0) arc (0:180:1.3 and 0.4);
\begin{scope}[yshift=1.6cm]
\curvedSolidTikz{1.3}{0.4}{1.9}
\end{scope}
\path (coneApex)--(coneRight) node[midway,right,xshift=5pt] {$l$};
\fill (0,0) circle (1.2pt);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0) -- (1.3,0) node[midway,below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$r$};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-1.7,0) -- (-1.7,1.6) node[midway,left] {$h$};
% Leaders are annotations, separate from the solid's edges.
\draw[-{Stealth}] (2.7,2.25) -- (0.8,1.9153);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (2.7,2.25) -- (1.0,1.3444);
\node[right] at (2.7,2.25) {faces that meet};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
A solid ornament consists of a hemisphere on a closed cylinder. Both have radius $3$ cm, and the cylinder is $5$ cm high. Find the total surface area, including the bottom, correct to $1$ decimal place.

Axial cross-section:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.2,0)--(-1.2,2)--(1.2,2)--(1.2,0)--cycle;
\draw (1.2,2) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.2];
\draw[dashed] (0,2)--(1.2,2);
\path (0.6,2) node[below] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\path (-1.2,1) node[left] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A solid model consists of a cone on a closed cylinder. Both have radius $2$ cm. The cylinder is $7$ cm high and the cone has slant height $6$ cm. Find the total surface area, including the bottom, correct to $1$ decimal place.

Axial cross-section:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1,0)--(-1,2)--(1,2)--(1,0)--cycle;
\draw (-1,2)--(0,4)--(1,2);
\path (0,2)--(1,2) node[midway,below] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\path (-1,1) node[left] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,4)--(1,2) node[midway,right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

An ice-cream shape consists of a hemisphere joined to a cone. Both have radius $4$ cm, and the cone has slant height $7$ cm. Find the total outside surface area in exact form, in terms of $\pi$.

